# Explore the reachable area and build a map of it, unattended.
#
# Goal
#
# max_duration_sec: give up and report what was mapped after this long.
#                   0 means no limit.
# min_frontier_size: ignore frontiers shorter than this, in metres. A finger's
#                    width of unknown behind a chair leg is not worth a trip.
#                    0 means use the node's own parameter.
# return_to_start: drive back to where exploration began once there is nothing
#                  left to explore.
float32 max_duration_sec
float32 min_frontier_size
bool return_to_start
---
# Result
#
# success is False for "stopped early" as well as for outright failure --
# message says which. explored_area_m2 counts free (driveable) cells only, not
# walls.
#
# frontiers_visited counts frontiers *dealt with*, which is not the same as
# trips completed: most frontiers stop existing because the robot mapped them
# on the way past, without ever arriving at them. Both endings count here,
# because both mean that piece of unknown is now known.
bool success
string message
uint32 frontiers_visited
float32 explored_area_m2
float32 duration_sec
---
# Feedback
#
# state: exploring | driving | returning | waiting_for_map | settling
# percent_explored: known cells as a share of the current map grid. The grid
#                   grows as SLAM discovers more, so this is a coverage
#                   readout, not a countdown to completion -- frontiers_remaining
#                   is the honest "how much is left".
# target_x/target_y: the frontier currently being driven to, in map metres.
#                    Both 0.0 when nothing is targeted.
string state
string message
uint32 frontiers_remaining
uint32 frontiers_visited
float32 explored_area_m2
float32 percent_explored
float32 distance_to_target
float32 target_x
float32 target_y
float32 elapsed_sec
